# Birmingham vs Coventry House Prices: 2000–2025

Which city experienced stronger house price growth over the past 25 years — Birmingham or Coventry?

Using HM Land Registry Price Paid Data, we analysed residential property transactions in both local authority districts between 2000 and 2025.

The results reveal an interesting difference.

- **Birmingham:** Average recorded sale prices increased from £74,458 in 2000 to £275,044 in 2025 — growth of approximately 269.4%.
- **Coventry:** Average recorded sale prices increased from £65,108 in 2000 to £254,514 in 2025 — growth of approximately 290.9%.

Although Birmingham had higher average transaction prices in both years, **Coventry experienced stronger percentage growth** over the 25-year period.

This article compares the two housing markets, examines their historical performance and considers what the differences may mean for property investors.

**Important:** These figures are nominal averages of recorded residential transactions, not a repeat-sales house price index. Changes in the types and locations of properties sold can affect the averages.


## Birmingham vs Coventry: House Price Growth Comparison

The table below compares average recorded residential sale prices in Birmingham and Coventry between 2000 and 2025.

| Measure | Birmingham | Coventry |
